{
  "id": "1CO.7",
  "number": "7",
  "bookId": "1CO",
  "reference": "1 Corinthians 7",
  "verseCount": 40,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "7",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "1CO 7"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "7",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now concerning the matters about which you wrote. It is well for a man not to touch a woman. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But because of the temptation to immorality, each man should have his own wife and each woman her own husband. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The husband should give to his wife her conjugal rights, and likewise the wife to her husband. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For the wife does not rule over her own body, but the husband does; likewise the husband does not rule over his own body, but the wife does. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "EXO.19.15"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ex 19.15",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Do not refuse one another except perhaps by agreement for a season, that you may devote yourselves to prayer; but then come together again, lest Satan tempt you through lack of self-control. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I say this by way of concession, not of command. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1CO.7.8"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "1 Cor 7.8",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1CO.9.5"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "9.5",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " I wish that all were as I myself am. But each has his own special gift from God, one of one kind and one of another.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.7"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "To the unmarried and the widows I say that it is well for them to remain single as I do. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1TI.5.14"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "1 Tim 5.14",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " But if they cannot exercise self-control, they should marry. For it is better to marry than to be aflame with passion.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.9"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "To the married I give charge, not I but the Lord, that the wife should not separate from her husband ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "(but if she does, let her remain single or else be reconciled to her husband)—and that the husband should not divorce his wife.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.11"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2CO.11.17"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "2 Cor 11.17",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " To the rest I say, not the Lord, that if any brother has a wife who is an unbeliever, and she consents to live with him, he should not divorce her. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If any woman has a husband who is an unbeliever, and he consents to live with her, she should not divorce him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For the unbelieving husband is consecrated through his wife, and the unbelieving wife is consecrated through her husband. Otherwise, your children would be unclean, but as it is they are holy. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But if the unbelieving partner desires to separate, let it be so; in such a case the brother or sister is not bound. For God has called us",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7.15",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Other ancient authorities read",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "you",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " to peace. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1PE.3.1"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "1 Pet 3.1",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Wife, how do you know whether you will save your husband? Husband, how do you know whether you will save your wife?",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "ROM.12.3"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Rom 12.3",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1CO.14.33"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "1 Cor 14.33",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2CO.8.18"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "2 Cor 8.18",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2CO.11.28"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "11.28",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Only, let every one lead the life which the Lord has assigned to him, and in which God has called him. This is my rule in all the churches. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1 Macc 1.15",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "ACT.15.1+ACT.15.2+ACT.15.3+ACT.15.4+ACT.15.5+ACT.15.6+ACT.15.7+ACT.15.8"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Acts 15.1-8",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Was any one at the time of his call already circumcised? Let him not seek to remove the marks of circumcision. Was any one at the time of his call uncircumcised? Let him not seek circumcision. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "GAL.5.6"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Gal 5.6",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "GAL.6.15"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "6.15",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "ROM.2.25"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Rom 2.25",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " For neither circumcision counts for anything nor uncircumcision, but keeping the commandments of God. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Every one should remain in the state in which he was called. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Were you a slave when called? Never mind. But if you can gain your freedom, avail yourself of the opportunity.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7.21",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Or",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "make use of your present condition instead",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "JHN.8.32"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Jn 8.32",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ",",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "JHN.8.36"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "36",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " For he who was called in the Lord as a slave is a freedman of the Lord. Likewise he who was free when called is a slave of Christ. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1CO.6.20"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "1 Cor 6.20",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " You were bought with a price; do not become slaves of men. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So, brethren, in whatever state each was called, there let him remain with God.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.24"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now concerning the unmarried,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7.25",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Greek",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "virgins",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " I have no command of the Lord, but I give my opinion as one who by the Lord's mercy is trustworthy. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I think that in view of the present",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7.26",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Or",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "impending",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " distress it is well for a person to remain as he is. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Are you bound to a wife? Do not seek to be free. Are you free from a wife? Do not seek marriage. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But if you marry, you do not sin, and if a girl",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7.28",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Greek",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "virgin",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " marries she does not sin. Yet those who marry will have worldly troubles, and I would spare you that. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "ROM.13.11+ROM.13.12"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Rom 13.11-12",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1CO.7.31"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "1 Cor 7.31",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " I mean, brethren, the appointed time has grown very short; from now on, let those who have wives live as though they had none, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and those who mourn as though they were not mourning, and those who rejoice as though they were not rejoicing, and those who buy as though they had no goods, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and those who deal with the world as though they had no dealings with it. For the form of this world is passing away.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.31"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.32"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1TI.5.5"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "1 Tim 5.5",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " I want you to be free from anxieties. The unmarried man is anxious about the affairs of the Lord, how to please the Lord; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.32"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "33",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:33"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "33",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "but the married man is anxious about worldly affairs, how to please his wife, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.33"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "34",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:34"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "34",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and his interests are divided. And the unmarried woman or girl",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.34",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.34"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7.34",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Greek",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "virgin",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " is anxious about the affairs of the Lord, how to be holy in body and spirit; but the married woman is anxious about worldly affairs, how to please her husband. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.34",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.34"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "35",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:35"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "35",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I say this for your own benefit, not to lay any restraint upon you, but to promote good order and to secure your undivided devotion to the Lord.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.35"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "35",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:35"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "35",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.35"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "36",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:36"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "36",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If any one thinks that he is not behaving properly toward his betrothed,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.36",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.36"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7.36",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Greek",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "virgin",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " if his passions are strong, and it has to be, let him do as he wishes: let them marry—it is no sin. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.36",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.36"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "37",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:37"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "37",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But whoever is firmly established in his heart, being under no necessity but having his desire under control, and has determined this in his heart, to keep her as his betrothed,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.37",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.37"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7.37",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Greek",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "virgin",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " he will do well. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.37",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.37"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "38",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CO 7:38"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "38",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So that he who marries his betrothed",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.38",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.38"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7.38",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Greek",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "virgin",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " does well; and he who refrains from marriage will do better.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CO.7.38",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CO.7.38"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
